  "name": "Public Administration and Constitutional Affairs Committee",
  "parent_committee_id": null,
  "purpose": "<p>The Public Administration and Constitutional Affairs Committee (PACAC) is appointed by the House of Commons to examine: constitutional issues; the quality and standards of administration provided by Civil Service departments; and the reports of the Public Service Ombudsman (PSO).</p>\r\n<p>Follow us on social media:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/hoccommittees.parliament.uk\">Bluesky</a> | <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61579513151155\">Facebook</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ukcommonscommittees\">Instagram</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/house-of-commons-committees\">LinkedIn</a> | <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/user/UKCommonsCommittees/\">Reddit</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/HoCcommitteesUK\">X</a> |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLj3mInRJqIekxA--aDW780T_TUCwjea4M\">YouTube</a></p>\r\n<p>Sign up to the <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/email/committeecorridor\">weekly cross-committee newsletter, ‘Committee Corridor’</a></p>",
